PROJECT PROMPT: SWASTHYASAATHI

Offline-First AI Companion for Frontline Healthcare Workers in Rural India

Act as a senior full-stack developer, AI/ML engineer, healthcare safety engineer, and product designer. Build a complete, functional, hackathon-ready prototype called SwasthyaSaathi — Reliable Health Guidance, Even Without a Network.

You must use the two provided project files as the primary source of requirements:

SwasthyaSaathi_NexGen_Presentation_Reversed.pptx — the product concept, workflows, proposed architecture, user interface, features, evaluation targets, and demonstration expectations.

H5_Frontline_Health_Worker_Companion_v1.0.zip — the authoritative problem statement, nine healthcare protocol documents, synthetic household register, ASHA worker data, development and test questions, baseline implementation, evaluation script, and submission specifications.

Do not build a generic healthcare chatbot. Implement the actual H5 problem and demonstrate the SwasthyaSaathi concept through a working application.

1. PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Develop a lightweight, offline-first healthcare companion for ASHA workers and ANMs working in rural Indian communities with unreliable internet connectivity and low-end Android devices.

The application must help frontline healthcare workers:

Ask questions about approved healthcare protocols using natural language, including Hinglish and supported Indian-language terms.

Receive answers grounded exclusively in the supplied protocol documents.

See citations identifying the exact protocol sections supporting each answer.

Detect predefined danger signs before any language-model reasoning.

Receive immediate referral guidance when a danger sign is detected.

Refuse questions outside the supplied protocol scope and redirect the worker to an appropriate doctor.

Generate a prioritized daily household visit list from the supplied synthetic household register.

Continue using its core functions without internet connectivity.

Store and retrieve data locally.

Measure its actual model footprint, memory consumption, and CPU response time.

Generate the three required H5 submission files in their exact specified formats.

The application must assist trained frontline healthcare workers. It must never present itself as an autonomous diagnostic system or a replacement for qualified medical professionals.

Project scenario

Use the fictional Chandrapuri Block described in the ZIP.

The scenario includes:

Five ASHA workers.

Six villages: Amrapur, Belwadi Tola, Kesarganj, Dhanpura, Navagaon Khurd, and Sitapahari.

Chandrapuri District Hospital as the referral hospital.

A synthetic household register containing 500 households and 2,234 household-member records.

Load these details from the supplied data files rather than inventing a separate dataset.

All names, households, villages, and healthcare records must be treated as synthetic demonstration data.

